# Instance configuration for multi-channel Claude Discord bot.
# Copy this file to instances.conf and fill in your Discord channel IDs.
#
# Format: instance_name  channel_id  working_directory
#
# - instance_name: used for tmux session name (claude-channel-<name>) and LaunchAgent label
#   Naming convention: use the directory path relative to ~, replacing / with -
#   (Discord channel names cannot contain / and -- is not allowed)
# - channel_id: Discord channel snowflake ID
# - working_directory: path where Claude Code runs (~ is expanded at install time)
#
# Each instance gets:
#   - Its own tmux session: claude-channel-<instance_name>
#   - Its own LaunchAgent: com.devin.claude-channel-<instance_name>
#   - Its own Discord state dir: ~/.claude/channels/discord-<instance_name>/
#     (with a per-instance access.json so it only listens to its channel)
#
# The bot process (single instance) routes commands to the correct tmux session
# based on which Discord channel the command was sent from.
#
# Example:
# home                1234567890123456789  ~/
# my-project          1234567890123456790  ~/my-project
# another-project     1234567890123456791  ~/another-project
